# The dungeon under Death House (death_house_dungeon_1): the family crypts, where the children can be laid to rest,
# the cult's ledger, and the Darklord's shrine (book area 31).

~ crypt_gustav
narrate examine:crypt_gustav
Narrator: A crypt cut with the name Gustav Durst and the year of his birth, its slab set ready and never closed. Nobody ever got around to dying properly.
if flag.death_house_dursts_destroyed
  Narrator: You know where he lies now, and someone should lay him in here. It won't be anyone in this house.
endif
-> END

~ crypt_elisabeth
narrate examine:crypt_elisabeth
Narrator: Elisabeth Durst's crypt, the slab still in place. The carving is the finest in the row, and something behind it is ticking, very faintly, like a great many small clocks.
if flag.death_house_insects_scattered
  Narrator: The coffin inside is empty and its lining eaten to lace. Nothing ticks now.
  -> END
endif
* Slide the slab aside. -> elisabeth_open
* [Nature DC 12] Listen to the ticking. -> elisabeth_listen | elisabeth_listen_fail
* Leave it shut. -> END

~ elisabeth_listen
Narrator: Mandibles. Thousands of them, working at wood and silk, in the dark where Elisabeth meant to lie. Whatever is in there has been eating for years.
-> elisabeth_choice

~ elisabeth_listen_fail
Narrator: A dry ticking, close behind the stone. It could be anything. It could be a great many anythings.
-> elisabeth_choice

~ elisabeth_choice
* Slide the slab aside. -> elisabeth_open
* Leave it shut. -> END

~ elisabeth_open
Narrator: The slab grinds aside, and the coffin's lid lifts by itself, raised from beneath by a pouring black tide of legs.
combat crypt_insects

~ crypt_children
narrate examine:crypt_children
if flag.death_house_children_at_rest
  Narrator: The two small crypts are closed now. Someone has scratched a little sun into each slab with the point of a knife.
  -> END
endif
Narrator: Two small crypts, carved Rosavalda and Thornboldt, with birth years and nothing after them. They stand open, swept and waiting.
if flag.death_house_children_remains_taken
  -> crypt_children_choice
endif
if flag.death_house_children_riding
  Narrator: From somewhere inside one of you, a small voice says: that's ours, but we're not in there. We're upstairs, in the toy chest.
endif
-> END

~ crypt_children_choice
* Lay the children's bones in their crypts. -> lay_to_rest
* Not yet. -> END

~ lay_to_rest
Narrator: You lay the two small bundles in their two small crypts and slide the slabs home. The sound is final and, for once in this house, kind.
if flag.death_house_children_riding
  Narrator: Two cold weights lift out of two of you, like children climbing down from a cart.
endif
Narrator: Rose and Thorn stand beside their crypts, clearer than you have ever seen them, and very calm.
Rose [smile]: It's quiet in here. Thank you. Thorn, say thank you.
Thorn: Thank you. Don't go downstairs.
Rose: Mother hid her purse under the bottom stair in the hall, under the loose board. She said it was for emergencies. I think this is one.
Rose: Goodbye. Properly, this time.
Narrator: Thorn waves. Then there is nobody to wave at.
set death_house_children_at_rest
set death_house_children_riding = false
quest rose_and_thorn at_rest
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: The dawn comes, little ones. Go on ahead of us. We'll follow one day, though not too soon.
if not flag.death_house_sacrificed
  interject name:thistle: Nobody left behind. Good.
endif
if not name:liriel_dawnsong
  interject class:cleric: Go gently. Nobody will lock that door again.
endif
approve liriel_dawnsong +4 godrick_pendlebrook +3 thistle +2 wren_featherfoot +2 kip_smudgewick +2 ratatoille +2: You laid Rose and Thorn to rest
inspire name:liriel_dawnsong: sent two children on toward the dawn
-> END

~ crypt_walter
narrate examine:crypt_walter
Narrator: The smallest crypt in the row says Walter, and nothing else: no family name, no dates. It has never been opened.
if flag.death_house_learned_walter
  Narrator: He never got a surname. He never got a birthday either.
endif
* [if flag.death_house_knows_lullaby] Hum the nursemaid's lullaby. -> walter_lullaby
* Move on. -> END

~ walter_lullaby
Narrator: The tune goes thin and strange in the stone gallery, and nothing answers. You decide that is the right answer.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: There. Somebody sang it for you. Sorry it took so long.
approve wren_featherfoot +2 liriel_dawnsong +1: You sang a forgotten baby his lullaby
-> END

~ cult_ledger
narrate examine:cult_ledger
Narrator: A ledger kept in a neat merchant's hand: dates, names, and beside each one the word given. Vagrants, a tinker, two pilgrims, a girl from Vallaki.
Narrator: The last entry is a single name, Walter. Where the others say given, it says first.
if not flag.death_house_read_cult_ledger
  set death_house_read_cult_ledger
  set death_house_lore += 1
endif
if not flag.death_house_learned_walter
  set death_house_learned_walter
  set death_house_lore += 1
endif
interject name:kip_smudgewick: That's a merchant's hand. Neat columns, every line tallied. They kept people like stock.
interject name:ratatoille: "Given." As if it were a pinch of salt. Mon dieu.
if not name:kip_smudgewick
  interject tag:scholarly: A ledger of the dead, kept neater than most temple records. That's the worst part.
endif
-> END

~ shrine_statue
narrate examine:shrine_statue
Narrator: A painted wooden statue of a gaunt, pale man in a black cloak, one hand resting on the head of a wolf at his side. The other holds out an orb of smoky crystal, as if offering it to whoever kneels here.
Narrator: Skeletons hang in rusty shackles around the walls, and the soot on the stones behind them is shaped like people.
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: So that's the lord of this place. He looks like a bully in a good coat.
if not name:godrick_pendlebrook
  interject class:cleric: A shrine to a lord, not a god. They knelt to the wrong one.
endif
if flag.death_house_took_shrine_orb
  Narrator: The statue's hand is empty now.
  -> END
endif
* [Arcana DC 12] Study the orb without touching it. -> orb_arcana | orb_arcana_fail
* Take the orb. -> orb_take
* Leave it be. -> END

~ orb_arcana
Narrator: Plain crystal, smoky and cold, worth a few coins: the magic in this room isn't in the orb. It is in the soot on the walls, and the soot is waiting for someone to take the offering.
-> orb_choice

~ orb_arcana_fail
Narrator: Smoky crystal, cold as a winter window. Whatever it is, it doesn't want to be understood.
-> orb_choice

~ orb_choice
* Take the orb anyway. -> orb_take
* Leave it be. -> END

~ orb_take
set death_house_took_shrine_orb
give arcane_focus_orb
Narrator: The orb comes away in {name}'s hand. Around the walls, the sooty shapes behind the skeletons peel themselves off the stone.
if not flag.death_house_shadows_destroyed
  combat shrine_shadows
endif
-> END
